Q: How to execute a query for each row of results from another query within a CodeIgniter view A: <p>The reality is that the <code>$this</code> variable is available in the view layer, so it is technically possible to interact with the database from the view (assuming the database library is already load) as follows.</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>foreach ($query-&gt;result() as $row):
   echo $row-&gt;post_title;
   echo $row-&gt;post_user_id;
   $user = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get_where('users', ['id' =&gt; $row-&gt;post_user_id])-&gt;row();
   echo $user-&gt;name ?? 'unknown';
   echo $user-&gt;location ?? 'unknown';
endforeach;
</code></pre>
<h2>However, no one should ever use the above approach!</h2>
<ol>
<li>Interacting with the database is the responsibility of the model layer.</li>
<li>A view shouldn't need to fetch or assemble or mutate any data. All data should be purposefully prepared before being sent to the view.</li>
<li>To understand all of the data that a view receives, a developer should be able to simply dump the $data variable from the controller or analyze that variable using IDE features.</li>
<li>The core reason to obey MVC best practices is for clarity and maintainability. When displayed data is not as expected, devs shouldn't need to check the view for processing bugs.</li>
<li>You already know that your view wants to present data from related rows in a second table. It absolutely is best practice to add a join clause to your query to append user details per post.</li>
</ol>
<p>Additional points:</p>
<ol>
<li>Contextually, the <code>Member</code> model doesn't sound like a class that should be querying a <em>posts</em> table.</li>
<li><code>select_sql()</code> is a very uninformative method name. A model method that <em>selects</em> data probably describes the majority of the methods in the model. If it only returns user data, then a better name might be <code>getUsers()</code>; for posts alone, <code>getPosts()</code>. It is common to append author details with a post. A method which appends author details could be called <code>getPostsWithAuthorDetails()</code></li>
<li>Your controller is not passing data to the view. I assume this is an error in your question rather than an error in your project code.</li>
<li>Layers outside of the model should not be responsible for mutating a CodeIgniter result set object into another structure. Unconditionally return an array of zero or more rows from your model method.</li>
</ol>
<p>Model:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function getPostsWithAuthorDetails(): array
{
    return $this-&gt;db
        -&gt;select('p.*, u.name, u.location')
        -&gt;join('users u', 'p.post_user_id = u.id')
        -&gt;order_by('p.post_date', 'desc')
        -&gt;get('posts p')
        -&gt;result();
}
</code></pre>
<p>Controller:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function posts()
{
    $this-&gt;load-&gt;model('Post_model', 'PostModel');
    $data['posts'] = $this-&gt;PostModel-&gt;getPostsWithAuthorDetails();
    $this-&gt;load-&gt;view('posts', $data);
}
</code></pre>
<p>View:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>foreach ($posts as $post) {
    echo &quot;$post-&gt;post_title; $post-&gt;post_user_id; $post-&gt;name; $post-&gt;location&quot;;
}
</code></pre>

Q: Text centered next to the image header A: <p>You can do this pretty easily with flexbox.</p>
<p>Set the header container to <code>display: flex</code> and use <code>align-items: center</code> to vertically center the text with the image:</p>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.header-container {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Then your HTML can stay roughly like this:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;header class=&quot;site-header&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;header-container&quot;&gt;
        &lt;img src=&quot;image/main/favicon.gif&quot; alt=&quot;Logo&quot; width=&quot;50&quot;&gt;

        &lt;h1&gt;Your Header Text&lt;/h1&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;
</code></pre>
<p><code>display: flex</code> puts the image and text next to each other, while <code>align-items: center</code> centers them vertically.</p>
<p>If you also want the whole group centered horizontally inside the header, you can add:</p>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.header-container {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 10px;
}
</code></pre>
<p>This avoids using margins or positioning just to align the text with the image.</p>

Q: Error when evaluating SSR module even when SSR is disabled - svelte-kit A: <p>At least nowadays (tested with SvelteKit 1.20.4), this works as advertised. Note that a few things in the question's example code were removed or are not necessary to solve the problem:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const config = {
    // ...
    kit: {
        ssr: false,
        prerender: {
            enabled: false
        },
        // ...
    }
};
</code></pre>
<p>These two options individually lead to the errors &quot;Unexpected option config.kit.ssr&quot; and &quot;Unexpected option config.kit.prerender.enabled&quot; respectively, and will abort the build.</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;script context=&quot;module&quot;&gt;
    export const ssr = false
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Independently of whether it's in the <code>module</code> script, this leads to the following warning: &quot;<code>export const ssr</code> will be ignored — move it to +page(.server).js/ts instead. See <a href="https://kit.svelte.dev/docs/page-options" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://kit.svelte.dev/docs/page-options</a> for more information.&quot;</p>
<p>The reason for requiring this is that reading the <code>ssr</code> property exported from some <code>+page.svelte</code> requires actually loading the component, including imports, at which point it is too late for preventing the issue.</p>
<p>If the export is moved to either of these files (<code>+page(.server).js/ts</code>), it will work. Steps to reproduce:</p>
<ul>
<li>create a new project (use demo app template): <code>npm create svelte@latest no-ssr-test &amp;&amp; cd no-ssr-test &amp;&amp; npm i</code></li>
<li>in <code>src/routes/+page.svelte</code>, insert <code>console.log(window)</code></li>
<li>run using <code>npm run dev</code> to verify you get <code>ReferenceError: window is not defined</code></li>
<li>in <code>src/routes/+page.js</code> (or similar), insert <code>export const ssr = false</code></li>
<li>run using <code>npm run dev</code> to verify the site works again</li>
</ul>

Q: Maven Nexus Issue - Authorization failed for 403 Forbidden A: <p>The issue at the time was with corporate proxy blocking download from maven central etc</p>
<p>Edit the proxies section in your maven settings.xml, which could be located in your ~/.m2/settings.xml file.
Settings.xml also exists in your MAVEN_HOME, so ensure you are updating the correct settings.xml</p>
<pre><code>&lt;settings&gt;
&lt;proxies&gt;
    &lt;proxy&gt;
        &lt;id&gt;httpproxy&lt;/id&gt;
        &lt;active&gt;true&lt;/active&gt;
        &lt;protocol&gt;http&lt;/protocol&gt;
        &lt;host&gt;your-proxy-host&lt;/host&gt;
        &lt;port&gt;your-proxy-port&lt;/port&gt;
        &lt;nonProxyHosts&gt;add.host.that.needs.to.bypass.proxy.here|some.host.com&lt;/nonProxyHosts&gt;
    &lt;/proxy&gt;
&lt;proxy&gt;
        &lt;id&gt;httpsproxy&lt;/id&gt;
        &lt;active&gt;true&lt;/active&gt;
        &lt;protocol&gt;https&lt;/protocol&gt;
        &lt;host&gt;your-proxy-host&lt;/host&gt;
        &lt;port&gt;your-proxy-port&lt;/port&gt;
        &lt;nonProxyHosts&gt;add.host.that.needs.to.bypass.proxy.here|some.host.com&lt;/nonProxyHosts&gt;
    &lt;/proxy&gt;

&lt;/proxies&gt;
&lt;/settings&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: How do you use the maven shade plugin to include only specific classes from a dependency with scope &quot;provided&quot;? A: <p>I had the same issue and fixed it by just changing the scope to compile</p>
<pre><code>&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.apache.tomcat&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;tomcat-catalina&lt;/artifactId&gt;
    &lt;version&gt;7.0.59&lt;/version&gt;
    &lt;scope&gt;compile&lt;/scope&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Now when you add the filter that includes only the class you care about, it will ignore everything else. Therefore, the shade plugin shouldn't include anything extra.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;build&gt;
    &lt;plugins&gt;
        &lt;plugin&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.apache.maven.plugins&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;maven-shade-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;version&gt;2.3&lt;/version&gt;
            &lt;executions&gt;
                &lt;execution&gt;
                    &lt;phase&gt;package&lt;/phase&gt;
                    &lt;goals&gt;
                        &lt;goal&gt;shade&lt;/goal&gt;
                    &lt;/goals&gt;
                    &lt;configuration&gt;
                        &lt;filters&gt;
                            &lt;filter&gt;
                                &lt;artifact&gt;org.apache.tomcat:tomcat-catalina&lt;/artifact&gt;
                                &lt;includes&gt;
                                    &lt;include&gt;org/apache/catalina/deploy/LoginConfig.class&lt;/include&gt;
                                &lt;/includes&gt;
                            &lt;/filter&gt;
                        &lt;/filters&gt;
                    &lt;/configuration&gt;
                &lt;/execution&gt;
            &lt;/executions&gt;
        &lt;/plugin&gt;
    &lt;/plugins&gt;
&lt;/build&gt;
</code></pre>
